<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Civil law</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Civil law is a legal tradition based on comprehensive written codes, derived ultimately from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a>. Its foundations lie in the law of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/corpus-juris-civilis">Corpus Juris Civilis</a> compiled in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleonic-code">Napoleonic Code</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> and the Austrian civil code of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> lands spread the tradition across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> and beyond.</p></div>
